decision_input_state_json:
{"choices":[{"label":"0","text":"Studies of invertebrates in the ocean have also found that in colder water and with higher oxygen content, the organisms there are also larger."},{"label":"1","text":"During the Carboniferous period, the concentration of oxygen in the earth ’s atmosphere was as high as 35%, much higher than the current 21%. At that time, there were many giant insects on the earth, and the wingspan of the dragonfly was close to one meter."},{"label":"2","text":"Small locusts cannot survive in a low-oxygen environment, especially in an environment with an oxygen concentration below 15%. Adult locusts can survive in an environment with 2% oxygen."},{"label":"3","text":"Under the environment with high oxygen content and high air pressure, the tested fruit flies lived to the fifth generation and their body size increased by 20%."}],"context":"Research has found that insects “breathe” through the stomata system on their bodies. The stomata are connected to the trachea, and more and more layers of smaller and smaller air are attached from top to bottom, thereby bringing oxygen to the whole body. At the current level of oxygen in the atmosphere, the total length of the stomata system has reached the limit; if the total length exceeds this limit, the oxygen supply capacity will be insufficient. Therefore, it can be judged that the amount of oxygen content can determine the size of insects.","poetic_rationale":"Insects breathe through stomata reaching a limit tied to our air,
So atmospheric oxygen levels cap how large these bugs can bear;
When Carboniferous oxygen soared to thirty-five percent long ago,
Giant dragonflies with one-meter wingspans proved this rule was so;
Thus history confirms the amount of oxygen determines insect size.","question":"Which of the following, if true, would best support the above argument?"}

{"choices":[{"label":"0","text":"Most of the nutrients people need are not from drinking water."},{"label":"1","text":"What the human body needs is not just minerals."},{"label":"2","text":"Drinking water other than pure water and mineral water."},{"label":"3","text":"People can get essential minerals from other foods."}],"context":"Compared with mineral water, pure water lacks minerals, and some of them are essential for the human body. Therefore, nutrition expert Lao Zhang suggested that those who regularly drink pure water change their habits and drink more mineral water.","poetic_rationale":"Lao Zhang advises switching from pure water because it lacks essential minerals found there,
Assuming we must obtain those vital elements specifically by drinking mineral water;
Yet option three shows people can get these essential minerals easily from other foods,
Removing the necessity to rely on water for the nutrients his reasoning includes,
Thus undermining his core premise and weakening his suggestion more than all the rest.","question":"Which of the following can weaken Lao Zhang ’s suggestion the most?"}

{"choices":[{"label":"0","text":"The vast majority of health care costs are spent on high-tech intensive care for high-risk patients."},{"label":"1","text":"Without increasing costs, our health conditions may also improve."},{"label":"2","text":"0% of the state's allocation to the health sector is for infrastructure construction."},{"label":"3","text":"The cost of care for elderly chronic diseases is very large."}],"context":"The report of the Ministry of Health shows that the cost of health care has indeed increased over the years. It can be seen that the medical conditions enjoyed by each of us have greatly improved.","poetic_rationale":"Rising costs are said to drive our improved health for all,
Yet most expense goes to high-risk care where few souls fall;
This concentrated spending on the severe and critical few
Disproves the claim that widespread better health is tied thereto,
As increased funds fail to show the general progress claimed.","question":"Which of the following raises the most serious question to the above conclusion?"}

{"choices":[{"label":"0","text":"Avoiding errors in vocabulary, grammar, and punctuation does not necessarily ensure the language quality of the manuscript."},{"label":"1","text":"Journalism courses have always emphasized and required students to be proficient in using computers and familiar with various software."},{"label":"2","text":"The more effective the Chinese software is, the more likely it is to be pirated."},{"label":"3","text":"Opening a new course at the School of Journalism requires a complicated process of argumentation and approval."}],"context":"There are more and more Chinese computer software that can correct vocabulary, grammar and punctuation are used incorrectly. Even if journalists do not have a good Chinese language foundation, they will not hinder writing. Therefore, schools that train journalists do not need to pay attention to the improvement of students 'Chinese ability, but should pay attention to the training of journalists' other qualities.","poetic_rationale":"Software fixes errors, so schools think language skills can fade,
Assuming correct mechanics mean good writing has been made;
Yet avoiding vocabulary and grammar mistakes does not ensure quality,
So software cannot justify ignoring a student's Chinese ability;
Thus journalism schools must still teach language proficiency.","question":"Which of the following, if true, would most weaken the above arguments and suggestions?"}

{"choices":[{"label":"0","text":"Among the patients who died above, the average year of death of the second group was two years earlier than the first group."},{"label":"1","text":"Among the patients who died, the average life span of the second group was two years shorter than that of the first group."},{"label":"2","text":"Among the above living patients, the second group is more severely ill than the first group."},{"label":"3","text":"Among the above living patients, the second group is older than the first group."}],"context":"There are 90 patients, all suffering from refractory disease T, who have taken the same conventional drugs. These patients were divided into two groups of equal numbers. The first group took W, an experimental drug used to treat T, and the second group took placebo without W. Statistics after 10 years show that 44 deaths occurred in both groups. Therefore, this test drug is ineffective.","poetic_rationale":"Equal deaths are claimed to show drug W is inert,
Yet Option Zero proves that death was still deferred;
The placebo group expired two prior years away,
So even without preventing death, the drug delayed decay;
Thus the proof of ineffectiveness melts entirely away.","question":"Which of the following, if true, would most weaken the above argument?"}

{"choices":[{"label":"0","text":"Some assistants to the general manager are in charge of the two departments."},{"label":"1","text":"Any department is in charge of F or G."},{"label":"2","text":"M and P are in charge of only one department."},{"label":"3","text":"No department is in charge of F, M and P."}],"context":"A company has six general manager assistants F, G, H, I, M and P, and three departments, each of which is in charge of three general manager assistants. Each assistant general manager is in charge of at least one department. The following conditions must be met? (1) There is only one assistant to the general manager in charge of three departments at the same time. (2) F and G are not in charge of the same department. (3) H and I are not in charge of the same department.","poetic_rationale":"Three departments total nine slots for six assistants to fill,
Where one singular person serves all three by strict rule.
Six slots still remain for the other five persons to take,
So an average above one forces extra assignments to wake;
Thus some assistants must manage exactly two departments still.","question":"Which of the following must be true?"}

{"choices":[{"label":"0","text":"Liu Dawei."},{"label":"1","text":"Li Qiang."},{"label":"2","text":"Wu Gang."},{"label":"3","text":"Wang Wei."}],"context":"Prince Lima in Li Na's mind is tall, handsome and doctor. She knew four men, Wang Wei, Wu Gang, Li Qiang, and Liu Dawei, and one of them met all the conditions she required. (1) Among the 4 men, there are 3 tall men, 2 doctors, and 1 is handsome; (2) Wang Wei and Wu Gang are both doctors; (3) Liu Dawei and Li Qiang are the same height; (4) Li Qiang and Wang Wei Not all are tall.","poetic_rationale":"Prince Lima must be tall, handsome, and a doctor too,
While Wang Wei and Wu Gang are the only two doctors in view.
Since Wang Wei and Li Qiang cannot both be tall, Wang Wei fails the height test;
Thus Wang Wei lacks the needed traits to pass the final quest.
This leaves Wu Gang as the single man who meets every required demand.","question":"Who can meet all the requirements of Li Na?"}

{"choices":[{"label":"0","text":"Tsinghua University Team."},{"label":"1","text":"China University of Science and Technology Team."},{"label":"2","text":"Zhejiang University Team."},{"label":"3","text":"Beijing University of Aeronautics and Astronautics."}],"context":"The football game in the "Master Cup 2003 China Robot Competition" is in progress. Three professors predicted the final result? Professor Zhao said? "The champion is not the Tsinghua University team nor the Zhejiang University team. " Professor Qian said ? "The champion is not the Tsinghua University team, but the University of Science and Technology of China. " Professor Sun said? "The champion is not the China University of Science and Technology team, but the Tsinghua University team. The results of the competition showed that only one of them judged both, one 'S judgment is one-to-one wrong, the other one is wrong.","poetic_rationale":"When Tsinghua is tested as the champion team,
Professor Sun gets both predictions right, as they seem;
Professor Qian is wholly wrong on every count,
While Zhao is half correct in the amount;
Thus matching the given rules, the winner is clear.","question":"According to the above situation, we know that the winner is."}

{"choices":[{"label":"0","text":"The scientist and one of the Americans are husband and wife."},{"label":"1","text":"The products of one of the entrepreneurs are mainly exported to the United States."},{"label":"2","text":"Two entrepreneurs are Chinese, and another American is a lawyer."},{"label":"3","text":"One of the lawyers is the legal adviser of one of the entrepreneurs."}],"context":"There are 9 passengers on a helicopter, including 1 scientist, 2 entrepreneurs, 2 lawyers, 3 Americans, and 4 Chinese.","poetic_rationale":"Summing listed identities yields twelve instead of nine,
Showing passenger categories must overlap and combine;
Option two resolves this by noting overlaps are met,
Where two Chinese entrepreneurs and one lawyer-American jet;
Twelve minus two entrepreneurs minus one lawyer leaves nine.","question":"Which of the following supplements can explain the inconsistency between the total number of people mentioned in the question stem and the number of people with different identities?"}

{"choices":[{"label":"0","text":"E."},{"label":"1","text":"G."},{"label":"2","text":"I."},{"label":"3","text":"K."}],"context":"There are 7 heart disease patients E, F, G, H, I, J, K to be assigned to 4 doctors for treatment, they are Dr. Zhang, Dr. Li, Dr. Wang and Dr. Liu. Only one doctor is responsible for each patient, and each doctor is responsible for the treatment of up to two patients. Among the patients, J and K are children, and the remaining 5 are adults; E, F, and J are males, and the remaining 4 are females. The following conditions must be met? (1) Dr. Zhang is only responsible for treating male patients. (2) Dr. Li can only be responsible for the treatment of 1 patient. (3) If a doctor is responsible for treating a child patient, then he must be responsible for the treatment of an adult patient of the same sex as the child.","poetic_rationale":"Dr. Li treats just one patient, yet child care demands
An adult of the same sex added to those healing hands,
For child J is a boy and child K is a girl,
Requiring a second adult matching each child's world;
Thus child K needs two spots and is barred from Dr. Li's care.","question":"Each of the following patients can be treated by Dr. Li, except which one?"}

{"choices":[{"label":"0","text":"In 1997, the "Hot Spring Xinjiang Northern Salamander Nature Reserve" was established, and local herders' awareness of protecting Xinjiang Northern Salamander is increasing."},{"label":"1","text":"In recent years, the rainfall has decreased and the groundwater level has fallen, which has affected the water source environment in which the northern salamander in Xinjiang lives."},{"label":"2","text":"Xinjiang salamander is a kind of animal that is afraid of light. Most of them hide under the rocks of the creek during the day, and avoid the trampling of cattle and sheep."},{"label":"3","text":"Xinjiang's northern salamanders are located in the mountains, and most tourists cannot enter at all."}],"context":"A rare and endangered animal of the northern salamander in Xinjiang. It was first discovered by a Russian explorer in 1840, but disappeared for more than 100 years. It was rediscovered in Hot Spring County, Xinjiang in 1898. But the data shows that in the 15 years since 1898, the number of northern salamanders in Xinjiang has been reduced by half. Some experts believe that the habitat of the northern salamander in Xinjiang was originally a local pasture, and the cattle and sheep walking around on the grassland in summer will trample them to death, resulting in a sharp decline in their numbers.","poetic_rationale":"Experts blame livestock trampling for the salamander's rapid population decline,
While Option One highlights falling groundwater and drought affecting their water source;
This introduces a different environmental cause that challenges the livestock threat,
Showing the habitat becomes uninhabitable rather than merely stepped on,
Thus raising the most doubt against the experts' singular assumption.","question":"Which of the following is true will raise the most doubts about the opinions of the above experts?"}

{"choices":[{"label":"0","text":"Triangles can be divided into three types? right triangle, obtuse triangle, and acute triangle. The sum of three internal angles of a right triangle is equal to 180 ℃, the sum of three internal angles of an obtuse triangle is equal to 180 ℃, and the sum of three internal angles of an acute triangle is equal to 180 ℃, so the sum of the triangles of all triangles is equal to 180 ℃."},{"label":"1","text":"I like "accidental" to "necessary". You see, the Olympic Games are full of suspense, so the competition is exciting; most of the artist ’s creations come from “spirit”. Scientists ’discoveries and inventions are often connected with“ intuition ”,“ epiphany ”and“ opportunity ”; in the vast crowd Occasionally and encounter "he" or "she", shoot each other Cupid's arrow, to achieve the best marriage in life. Therefore, I love "accidental", I want to shout "Long live accidental"!"},{"label":"2","text":"Surgeons can see X-rays when performing surgery on patients, lawyers can view defense books when defending defendants, architects can compare design drawings when building a house, and teachers can read various reference books for class preparation. Why are students not allowed to Reading textbooks and other relevant materials during the exam?"},{"label":"3","text":"The roses are beautiful because all the words are beautiful."}],"context":"Wedding seeing, love seeing; love letter seeing, missing seeing, flower seeing, spring seeing; fruit seeing, nutrition seeing; helping seeing, caring seeing; windy seeing The air is invisible; the diploma is invisible and the level is invisible. Someone concluded from this that things that are invisible are more valuable than things that are visible.","poetic_rationale":"Invisible things like air are linked to value,
Just as option one ties the accidental to success;
Both list diverse examples to build a wide generalization,
Drawing a subjective, flawed conclusion from limited pairs,
Thus option one alone replicates the passage's inductive leap.","question":"Which of the following options uses the same reasoning method as in the question stem?"}

{"choices":[{"label":"0","text":"Cars drive faster on long streets than on short streets, so pedestrians on long streets are more dangerous than pedestrians on short streets."},{"label":"1","text":"Many people who later become entrepreneurs often participate in competitive sports when they are in college. Therefore, participation in competitive sports must promote the ability to make people entrepreneurs."},{"label":"2","text":"The petals of mulberry chrysanthemum will be closed at noon, so the petals of mulberry chrysanthemum will definitely open at night."},{"label":"3","text":"The events in Eastern Europe will affect the political situation in Central America, so the liberalization of Eastern Europe will lead to the liberalization of Central America."}],"context":"The hurricane that threatened the continental United States was triggered by the high pressure on the west coast of Africa. Whenever there is heavy rainfall in the area south of the Sahara Desert, the continental United States will be hit by a particularly frequent hurricane. Therefore, a large amount of rainfall must be the cause of the hurricane that increases the pressure of the airflow.","poetic_rationale":"Africa's heavy rains and storms are seen to meet,
Concluding that the rainfall caused the driving heat;
When sports and future entrepreneurs are linked in sight,
We wrongly claim that playing makes their business bright.
Both match by twisting mere correlation into cause.","question":"Which of the following arguments contains defects most similar to those in the above argument?"}

{"choices":[{"label":"0","text":"The greatest philosophers in the world prefer to avoid intimate relationships."},{"label":"1","text":"People with intimate relationships rarely spend their time alone."},{"label":"2","text":"Loneliness is necessary for philosophers to meditate."},{"label":"3","text":"The greatest philosophers in the world are happy."}],"context":"There is a psychological theory that to be happy, one must maintain an intimate relationship with another. However, the greatest philosophers in the world spent most of their lives in isolation, and had no intimate relationships. Therefore, this psychological theory must be wrong.","poetic_rationale":"To find true joy, a theory says we need an intimate bond,
Yet history's greatest thinkers lived in isolation far beyond.
If lack of deep connection proves that happiness can still be found,
Then those wise minds must truly have with happiness been crowned;
For if they weren't content, this theory would remain quite sound.","question":"Which of the following must be assumed in the above conclusion?"}

{"choices":[{"label":"0","text":"E, F, H, K."},{"label":"1","text":"E, H, J, M."},{"label":"2","text":"E, G, J, M."},{"label":"3","text":"F, H, K, M."}],"context":"A provincial Go team coach selects 4 of the 7 players from E, F, G, H, J, K and M to participate in the professional league. The selection must meet the following conditions? E or F has one person to participate, but not both . One of J or K will participate, but not both. If J participates, then G participates. Unless F participates, M does not participate.","poetic_rationale":"While E and F, and J and K, divide their pairs apart,
If J plays, G joins too, and M needs F to take his part;
Options zero, one, and two break rules of M, E, or F,
While checking option three leaves every single mandate met,
So F, H, K, and M alone fulfill the proper chart.","question":"Which of the following four players can participate in the game together?"}

{"choices":[{"label":"0","text":"If a person is careful, he has no taste."},{"label":"1","text":"If a person is overbearing, he is immoral."},{"label":"2","text":"If humans plunder nature, there will be no sustainable life."},{"label":"3","text":"If a person is immoral, he is overbearing and careful."}],"context":"Culture is reflected in how a person treats himself, others, and the natural environment in which he lives. In a society with a solid cultural environment, people know how to respect themselves-he is meticulous and meticulous and has taste; people know how to respect others-he is not overbearing and morality is not overbearing; people know how to respect nature-he does not rob Only if you do not plunder do you have a sustainable life.","poetic_rationale":"Respect brings meticulous taste and moral grace,
While overbearing actions show a lack of place;
Plundering nature destroys our sustainable life ahead,
Linking immorality and overbearingness is what is said;
Thus coupling immorality with carefulness cannot be read.","question":"Which of the following cannot be derived from the above sentence?"}

{"choices":[{"label":"0","text":"The change of the problem means that the transition from the competition of the enterprise to the competition of the industry."},{"label":"1","text":"Only by being the best can companies make big money."},{"label":"2","text":"Only in a profitable industry can we do our best."},{"label":"3","text":"What used to be good or bad in the industry is now only good or bad for enterprises."}],"context":"The question of all enterprises in the past was such a question; "What should I do, what can I do to make money?" After joining the WTO, the question becomes? "What can I do to be the best?".","poetic_rationale":"Before the WTO, businesses asked how to make money,
Tying success directly to overall industry gains;
Now the question is solely how to be the best,
Where performance shifts from the whole sector to individual firms;
Thus what once was judged by the industry is now judged by the enterprise.","question":"Which of the following statements gives the most reasonable explanation for the change in the above problem?"}

{"choices":[{"label":"0","text":"Kinship can be built not only on the foundation of private morality, but also on the foundation of public morality."},{"label":"1","text":"The main function of the system is to dilute family relationships and prevent people from using them to do bad things."},{"label":"2","text":"Affection can bring efficiency to the enterprise, and once it is turned into hatred, it can also bring disaster to the enterprise."},{"label":"3","text":"Although the system can inspire affection, the system itself cannot tolerate any kind of affection."}],"context":"Enterprise competition is based on efficiency, and efficiency is based on family. The various systems in our country are not intended to destroy family relationships, but to maximize family relationships.","poetic_rationale":"Efficiency stems from family, systems maximize these ties,
Yet Option One asserts the system's true role lies
In diluting family bonds to stop corrupt design,
Directly crushing the text's core supporting line;
Thus this choice defeats the claim that systems make them rise.","question":"If the following statement is true, which one will weaken the above conclusion most seriously?"}

{"choices":[{"label":"0","text":"China's current CPI statistical range and standards were formulated more than 20 years ago, and it is difficult to truly reflect the current trend of consumer prices."},{"label":"1","text":"The CPI published by the National Bureau of Statistics is a data description of the overall situation of the prices of various goods and services across the country, and it cannot fully reflect individual feelings and the differences between regions and consumption levels."},{"label":"2","text":"Products with a high degree of relevance to people's lives tend to increase prices; those with a low degree of relevance tend to fall prices."},{"label":"3","text":"High-income groups have little sense of a small price increase."}],"context":"Last year, the national consumer price index (CPI) rose only 1.8%, which is a moderate increase. However, people's personal feelings are quite different. They feel that water, electricity, gas, vegetables, oil, going to school to see a doctor, and buying a house by car are all rising prices, and the increase is not "moderate. ".","poetic_rationale":"Outdated indexes and broad national averages fail to match daily life,
While essential goods rise and hidden drops distort the broader view.
Yet high-income groups alone cannot define the public grief,
Since wealthy indifference leaves the widespread feeling unexplained;
Thus, that narrow focus fails to bridge the gap between stats and truth.","question":"Which of the following options does not help explain the gap between the statistics in the question and the people ’s feelings?"}

{"choices":[{"label":"0","text":"In the past 10 years, children's physical activity in Beijing has become less and less."},{"label":"1","text":"In the past 10 years, the number of non-obese children in Beijing has also continued to rise."},{"label":"2","text":"In the past 10 years, the number of obese children in Beijing's urban areas has also continued to decrease."},{"label":"3","text":"Children in Beijing ’s urban area become more likely to gain weight as they age."}],"context":"According to the conclusions of the four main surveys conducted in the past 10 years, the number of obese children in the urban area of ​​Beijing has been continuously increasing with the weight of children over 85% of the same age as the standard of obesity.","poetic_rationale":"Four surveys show urban Beijing's obese kids grew for ten years straight,
While overall child population counts remained stable or did not abate;
Because the total sum comprises obese and non-obese children combined,
A rising obese group means non-obese kids must also increase in kind;
Thus, the number of non-obese children in Beijing has likewise continued to rise.","question":"If the findings in the above survey are correct, which of the following conclusions can be drawn based on this?"}

{"choices":[{"label":"0","text":"India is one of the cultural districts during the cultural axis period."},{"label":"1","text":"Greece is one of the cultural districts during the cultural axis period."},{"label":"2","text":"China is one of the cultural districts during the cultural axis period."},{"label":"3","text":"Egypt is one of the cultural districts during the cultural axis period."}],"context":"There is a European-centric bias in the perception of world culture. During the period of the cultural axis, every cultural area has its backbone thoughts, and each backbone thought has its contribution to world culture. The backbone of China's ideology is both Confucianism, Taoism, and Mohism, and the ideas of the sons represented by Confucianism, Taoism, and Moth have contributed to world culture.","poetic_rationale":"To counter European bias, the argument claims
every cultural axis area contributes its backbone thoughts.
It cites China's Confucian, Taoist, and Mohist ideals
to prove that specific region's global cultural worth;
thus, China must be a cultural district in that era.","question":"Which of the following statements is the assumption upon which the above argument relies?"}

{"choices":[{"label":"0","text":"Welfare distribution is cancelled, and the surplus of money in the hands of residents increases, resulting in a strong demand for house purchases."},{"label":"1","text":"It is impossible for the government to restrain house prices excessively, because that will severely hit the housing industry, leading to many risks such as finance and employment."},{"label":"2","text":"The price of affordable housing is still too high for some socially disadvantaged groups."},{"label":"3","text":"China has limited land resources, and the government must strictly control the supply of land used for building houses."}],"context":"In recent years, although the government has taken many measures to curb housing prices, housing prices are still rising rapidly, and this situation cannot be fundamentally changed in the short term.","poetic_rationale":"Despite state efforts, home prices still ascend,
High demand and scarce land make the trend extend,
While economic risks limit government control,
High prices persist as a stubborn whole;
Option two shows hardship, but proves no market trend.","question":"The following options all support the point of view in the question, except?"}

{"choices":[{"label":"0","text":"E is somewhere north of G."},{"label":"1","text":"F is somewhere north of I."},{"label":"2","text":"G is somewhere north of E."},{"label":"3","text":"I is somewhere north of F."}],"context":"There are five volcanic islands E, F, G, H, and I in the east coast of a country. They are arranged in a straight line from north to south, and they are found? (1) F is adjacent to H and is on the north side of H. (2) I and E are adjacent. (3) G is somewhere in the north of F.","poetic_rationale":"With F north of H, and G north of them all,
G is adjacent to E, preventing E's fall;
Since E cannot slide south of F, it rests north,
And adjacent I must precede E forth;
Thus I sits above F, answering the call.","question":"If G and E are adjacent, which of the following statements must be true?"}

{"choices":[{"label":"0","text":""No time to read" is the main reason for the decline in book reading."},{"label":"1","text":"The online reading rate of our nationals has increased from 3.7% in 1999 to 27.8% in 2005."},{"label":"2","text":"In recent years, China's book publishing has problems such as high book prices, tedious content, and excessive hype."},{"label":"3","text":"You can also learn a lot by listening to lectures."}],"context":"A survey shows that the national book reading rate of our country has been declining for 6 consecutive years. In 2005, the national book reading rate was lower than 50% for the first time.","poetic_rationale":"Though physical book reading rates have fallen year by year,
Online reading rates have surged from past years to the present;
This shift in formats proves that people read elsewhere,
While book publishing flaws and lack of time are not the key,
Online reading solves the paradox of where our readers went.","question":"Which of the following, if true, can explain the above contradiction?"}

{"choices":[{"label":"0","text":"A good natural environment is more important for people in developed countries than people in developing countries."},{"label":"1","text":"Both developed and developing countries have polluting enterprises."},{"label":"2","text":"The degree of environmental pollution in developed countries is more serious than in developing countries."},{"label":"3","text":"Polluting industries can generate more profits in developing countries than in developed countries."}],"context":"An economist suggested that when transferring polluting industries from developed countries to developing countries, developed countries benefited from the improvement of the natural environment; although the developing countries were polluted by the environment, they were compensated for solving employment and increasing taxes. As a result, the situation on both sides has improved, resulting in an increase in total global welfare.","poetic_rationale":"Industries of pollution shift from rich to poor lands,
Bringing cleaner nature north while jobs and taxes grace the south,
Where mutual gains increase the total global welfare;
This trade relies upon the hidden premise that green spaces
Matter more to developed homes than to developing nations.","question":"Which of the following is the hypothesis discussed by the economist?"}

{"choices":[{"label":"0","text":"The earliest stars contained only hydrogen."},{"label":"1","text":"When the universe was less than 1.5 billion years old, some stars had already formed."},{"label":"2","text":"This nebula also contains hydrogen and helium."},{"label":"3","text":"The carbon in this nebula later formed part of some stars."}],"context":"The early universe contained only the lightest elements? hydrogen and helium. Heavier elements like carbon can only be formed in the star's nuclear reaction and diffuse when the star explodes. A nebula recently discovered contained carbon formed billions of years ago, when the universe was no more than 1.5 billion years old.","poetic_rationale":"In early times, but lightest gases grew,
While carbon needs a star's hot core to brew;
A nebula holds carbon formed of old,
When youth of space had 1.5 billions told;
Thus stars had formed before that time took place.","question":"If the above statement is true, which of the following must be true?"}

{"choices":[{"label":"0","text":"A pianist at the concert should not take a completely negative view of the mistakes that occurred in the difficult performance, and understand why the mistakes occurred, so that the pianist can make better preparations for future performances."},{"label":"1","text":"A salesperson should understand that the commission earned is not only a reward for the sales transaction, but also should be satisfied by the personality charm they show in the sales transaction."},{"label":"2","text":"Compassion is very valuable, not only because it can bring people a good feeling, but also it can bring some opportunities to enrich the lives of others."},{"label":"3","text":"Even if you are afraid to speak in public, you should accept the invitation to speak in front of the masses. People will admire your courage, and you can also get a sense of satisfaction in accomplishing things that you cannot accomplish."}],"context":"Challenges are an important source of self-knowledge, because those who pay attention to how they respond emotionally and physically when accepting challenges can more effectively gain insight into their weaknesses.","poetic_rationale":"Challenges teach us deep self-knowledge when we watch our reactions grow,
While options missing trials or fears fail to reveal what we must know;
So facing public speaking fears lets one confront emotional strain,
Since only meeting trials head-on brings insight through the pain;
Thus choosing challenges to face is how true weakness comes to light.","question":"Which of the following is most consistent with the principles discussed above?"}

{"choices":[{"label":"0","text":"Wang Ying can speak English, and Wang Ying is Chinese, so Chinese can speak English."},{"label":"1","text":"The Ministry of Education stipulates that colleges and universities are not allowed to engage in stock investment, so Professor Zhang of Peking University cannot buy stocks."},{"label":"2","text":"The Chinese Olympic Committee is a member of the International Olympic Committee, and Mr. Y is a member of the Chinese Olympic Committee. Therefore, Mr. Y is a member of the International Olympic Committee."},{"label":"3","text":"Our school games are the sports games of the whole school, and the Olympic Games are the sports games all over the world; students of our school must participate in the opening ceremony of the Universiade. Therefore, people all over the world must participate in the opening ceremony of the Olympic Games."}],"context":"Five former Chinese workers who were caught in Japan during the Japanese invasion of China sued a Japanese company for damages. In its final judgment in 2007, the Supreme Court of Japan claimed that, according to the "Sino-Japanese Joint Statement," the Chinese people's right to individual claims had been waived, and therefore the Chinese laborers' claims were rejected. The "Sino-Japanese Joint Statement" signed in 1972 was written like this? "The government of the People's Republic of China announced that it would abandon its war compensation claims against the Japanese for the friendship of the Chinese and Japanese people. ".","poetic_rationale":"The Chinese state waived all its claims,
So individual laborers lost their aims;
When colleges are banned from stocks,
Professor Zhang must yield to rules and locks;
A collective's rule on members falls.","question":"Which of the following is the same as the method of argument of the Japanese Supreme Court?"}

{"choices":[{"label":"0","text":"This country can either maintain its economic development or maintain its social stability."},{"label":"1","text":"If we reduce the proportion of companies paying social insurance premiums for employees each year, we can maintain the competitiveness of the company."},{"label":"2","text":"This country cannot maintain its economic development or maintain its social stability."},{"label":"3","text":"The economic development of this country will be affected to a certain extent."}],"context":"The problem faced by a developing country is that to maintain its economic development, it must constantly strengthen the competitiveness of domestic enterprises; to maintain social stability, it must constantly establish and improve social security systems such as pensions, medical care, and unemployment. To establish and improve the social security system, enterprises need to pay a certain percentage of social insurance premiums for employees every year. If an enterprise pays such a proportion of social insurance premiums for employees every year, it will reduce the competitiveness of the enterprise.","poetic_rationale":"Economic growth requires that enterprises stay strongly competitive,
While social stability demands funding welfare through insurance fees.
Yet business payments toward such security reduce enterprise competitiveness,
Creating a direct conflict where achieving both aims is mutually blocked;
Thus the nation cannot maintain its economic development and social stability.","question":"Which of the following conclusions can be derived from the above statement?"}

{"choices":[{"label":"0","text":"Ignore this possibility? if Zhang Wei had to give a class report, then her semester papers would not get an excellent result."},{"label":"1","text":"This possibility was not taken into account? some students had excellent semester thesis but failed the exam."},{"label":"2","text":"Ignore this possibility? Zhang Wei's semester papers must be excellent, otherwise a class report will be required."},{"label":"3","text":"Relying on unconfirmed assumptions? If Zhang Wei's semester papers are not excellent, she will fail the exam without giving a lecture."}],"context":"All of Zhang Wei ’s extracurricular assignments are excellent. If her semester papers are also excellent, she can pass the exam even if she does not make a class report. Unfortunately, her semester dissertation did not get an excellent grade, so she had to give a lecture in order to pass the exam.","poetic_rationale":"Her top papers merely mean she skips a talk to pass,
Yet the passage leaps to claim she needs that speech *alas*;
