{"choices":[{"label":"0","text":"In the traditional cod fishing belt, a large number of seals caused great inconvenience to the fishing boat."},{"label":"1","text":"The damage caused by seawater pollution to cod is more serious than that caused to seals."},{"label":"2","text":"Before the number of seals increased, the number of cod in the North Atlantic Ocean was greatly reduced."},{"label":"3","text":"Cod almost only eat capelin, and this fish is also the main food for seals."}],"context":"When the number of cod in the North Atlantic Ocean decreased significantly, the number of seals increased from 1.5 million to about 2.5 million. Some people think that seals have caused a decrease in cod, but seals rarely eat cod, so it is unlikely that a large increase in the number of seals caused a significant decline in the number of cod.","poetic_rationale":"Seals rarely eat cod, assuming no direct harm,
