This proves that word reactions do not depend on meaning alone,
For pronunciation's separate influence is thus shown;
Thus, meaningless words act as a premise for this claim.","question":"A lot of meaningless words can cause people to respond positively or negatively. " Which of the following roles does this assertion play in the above argument?"}

{"choices":[{"label":"0","text":"In the past two years, the incidence of bladder cancer among Dutch dairy cow and dairy consumers has been particularly high."},{"label":"1","text":"Biphenyl residues have been found in the blood and urine of many Dutch cows."},{"label":"2","text":"The incidence of cancer in the dairy production areas of the Netherlands ranks first in the country."},{"label":"3","text":"The infertility rate of Dutch cows is higher than the average of other cows."}],"context":"In recent years, experts have called for a ban on the addition of biphenyl compounds as oxytocin to animal feed, because this substance is harmful to humans. In the past ten years, it has been found that the residues of biphenyls in the feeds of many Dutch dairy cows raised by herders.","poetic_rationale":"Experts seek to ban biphenyl feed,
