{"choices":[{"label":"0","text":"A is not a fish thief."},{"label":"1","text":"B is not a fish thief."},{"label":"2","text":"C speak the truth."},{"label":"3","text":"Ding tells lies."}],"context":"A family has four cats, one of them steals the fish from his family. The host interrogated them, and only one cat told the truth. The four cats answered as follows? A? "B is a fish thief. " B? "C is a fish thief. " C? "A or B is a fish thief. " D? "B or C is a fish thief. " . ".","poetic_rationale":"When cat A is assumed as the sole fish thief,
