{"choices":[{"label":"0","text":"Depression is not only a mental illness, but also an organic disease."},{"label":"1","text":"It may be that depression leads to an imbalance in the concentration of these three neurotransmitters in the brain."},{"label":"2","text":"Women and the elderly are high-risk groups of depression."},{"label":"3","text":"Drugs developed for the above three neurotransmitters to maintain their concentration balance are effective in treating depression."}],"context":"People with depression have a strong tendency to commit suicide. Many people think that depression is a psychological disease. In the mid-20th century, medical research found that there are 3 neurotransmitters (serotonin, nor-nor The concentration of epinephrine and dopamine is lower than that of normal people. Medical scientists speculate that the imbalance of these three neurotransmitters caused depression.","poetic_rationale":"Low brain neurotransmitters are thought to cause depression's plight,
While rival claims or mere disease labels leave the link unclear;
Yet when targeted drugs successfully cure the condition outright,
