{"choices":[{"label":"0","text":"The price of ordinary vegetables in Japan is not too high."},{"label":"1","text":"Chinese people's general concerns about food safety have led to a shortage of organic vegetables."},{"label":"2","text":"Chinese organic vegetables are no more expensive than Japanese organic vegetables."},{"label":"3","text":"The price of ordinary vegetables in China is completely marketized, and the profit margin is normal."}],"context":"The certification conditions for organic vegetables in Japan are very harsh, requiring that the land where organic vegetables are grown have not used any pesticides or fertilizers within 3 years. The selling price of Japanese organic vegetables is only 20% -30% higher than ordinary vegetables. In China, the price of organic vegetables is several times or even 10 times that of ordinary vegetables. This shows that China's organic vegetable cultivation industry is a huge profit industry.","poetic_rationale":"Japan’s strict organic rules keep their green prices low,
