{"choices":[{"label":"0","text":"Of the approximately 1 million English words, although only a dozen are swear words, they are used very frequently."},{"label":"1","text":"Research by brain scientists confirmed that the human spirit can change the state of the body in a physiological sense."},{"label":"2","text":"Swearing is the most expressive word for extreme emotions. Swearing can reduce stress and help to endure pain."},{"label":"3","text":"General words are stored in the upper brain area that controls autonomous behavior and rational thinking, while swear words are stored in the lower brain area responsible for emotions and instincts."}],"context":"Dr. Melissa Moore of Stanford University in the United States? "Oh My God? A Brief History of Swearing" talked about an interesting phenomenon? some patients with Alzheimer's disease or stroke have completely lost their language ability , Can still say a certain swear word repeatedly. This is confusing? aren't swear words talking?","poetic_rationale":"General words live high where reason holds sway,
