As changing evaluations for the same art prove this shift;
Thus lasting joy reveals a truly great and objective work.","question":"Which of the following statements best supports the above statement?"}

{"choices":[{"label":"0","text":"Freedom of expression is not sufficient to meet the needs of the people, and good social order is also indispensable."},{"label":"1","text":"The legitimate function of the government is not to meet the needs of the people, but to provide the people with equal opportunities."},{"label":"2","text":"Government officials are diligent and loyal to the people and do their due diligence. They already know what the people need and are dissatisfied."},{"label":"3","text":"Free speech leads to a lot of noise and is easy to disrupt the social order, and good social order is a prerequisite for the government to meet the needs of the people."}],"context":"The function of the government is to satisfy the real needs of the people. Unless the government knows what the people really need, the government cannot meet those needs. Free speech can ensure that government officials hear such demand information. Therefore, for a healthy country, free speech is essential.","poetic_rationale":"To satisfy real needs is government's true role,
