Though other needs matter, option zero leaves this core clear.","question":"If the following statement is true, which one cannot weaken the conclusion of the above argument?"}

{"choices":[{"label":"0","text":"If Russia introduces foreign capital and labor into the Far East, the region will be revitalized."},{"label":"1","text":"If Russia can realize the revitalization of the Far East by its own strength, the region will not be "alienated" by foreign immigrants."},{"label":"2","text":"If Russia continues to improve its systems while introducing foreign capital and labor into the Far East, the region will not be "alienated" by foreign immigrants."},{"label":"3","text":"If you want to rejuvenate the Far East without relying on your own strength, Russia will face the question that the region may be "alienated" by foreign immigrants."}],"context":"At present, the utilization rate of cultivated land in Russia in the Far East is less than 50%. The Russian Ministry of Economic Development intends to lease agricultural land to Asia-Pacific countries for a long time. The Ministry believes that if there is no foreign capital and labor injection, Russia cannot rely on its own power to achieve the revitalization of the Far East. However, if foreign capital and labor enter the Far East, the area may be alienated by foreign immigrants.","poetic_rationale":"Without foreign help, Russia cannot revive its Far East land,
